      "supporting_quotes": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-94fb33e0def3",
          "exact": "Taking base-2 logarithms of both sides of the exposure equation and separating numerators and denominators reduces exposure calculation to a matter of addition: Ev = Av + Tv = Bv + Sv, where Av is the aperture value, Tv is the time value, Sv is the speed value (aka sensitivity value), and Bv is the luminance value (aka brightness value)."
        }
      ],
      "observations": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-94fb33e0def3",
          "subject": "exposure calculation",
          "predicate": "reduces to addition via base-2 logarithms as",
          "object": "Ev = Av + Tv = Bv + Sv (Av aperture value, Tv time value, Sv speed/sensitivity value, Bv luminance/brightness value)"
        }
      ],
      "applied_rule_refs": [
        "VAL-001",
        "VAL-002"
      ],
      "rationale": "引文[0,160)说明对曝光方程两边取以 2 为底对数并分离分子分母后，曝光计算化为加法；[161,184)给出 Ev = Av + Tv = Bv + Sv；[191,216)/[217,238)/[239,285)/[290,339)分别对应 Av（光圈值）、Tv（时间值）、Sv（感光值，aka 灵敏度值）、Bv（亮度值，aka 明度值）。与 claim 逐项对应。",
